{
  "version": "som.typescript-catalog.v1",
  "dsl_version": "som.dsl.typescript.v1",
  "rule": "The plan for a prompt keeps, in this order, every file and every block whose versions list the prompt version. There are no when conditions in phase 1: every admitted prompt has the one product-layout.json shape, and /healthz is refused as a resource path. A DSL block has only id, name, params and refs. A block param {\"$ref\": \"a.b\"} names the prompt value at /a/b. refs name blocks of the same file. A file path names the prompt value in braces. Every block id starts with ts. and is rendered by the TypeScript block library. Block names and params mirror the Rust phase 1 resource blocks of the same role, so a prompt has the same block names in both targets. The Rust src/models.rs row blocks have no TypeScript file: the read interface in src/schemas.ts is also the row type. The Rust src/lib.rs block becomes src/migrate.ts, the hand-written migrator.",
